      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U10", "U11"],
      "pins": ["U10.4", "U10.5", "U11.4", "U11.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "Both ground pins of each isolated CAN transceiver are connected to the same GND net. The transceivers’ isolated-side supplies are also on 5V_switched_CAN, which is switched from the board’s +5V rail through Q9.",
      "expected": "For the specified isolated CAN interfaces, the bus-side supply and return must be galvanically isolated from the logic-side supply and return.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "GND: ... U10.4(GND1,power_in) U10.5(GND2,power_in) ... U11.4(GND1,power_in) U11.5(GND2,power_in)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "5V_switched_CAN: ... Q9.3(D,passive) U10.8(VCC2,power_in) U11.8(VCC2,power_in)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The CAN interfaces do not provide galvanic isolation as specified, so ground offsets or faults on the bus side can couple into the logic-side ground and electronics.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["U15", "U22", "U35", "U36"],
      "pins": ["U15.1", "U15.2", "U15.4", "U22.1", "U22.4", "U35.1", "U35.2", "U35.4", "U36.1", "U36.2", "U36.4"],
      "nets": ["ESTOP_SINK1", "ESTOP_SINK2", "ESTOP_SINK_LOCAL", "ESTOP_SINK_ALL", "ESTOP_OUT", "ESTOP"],
      "observed": "These e-stop buffers are valued SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1, but their sourcing MPN is U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R. The 1G125 is a tri-state push-pull buffer, not the open-drain 1G07 specified.",
      "expected": "Use the specified SN74LVC1G07 open-drain buffer, or otherwise ensure the sourced part’s output behavior matches the intended e-stop sink circuit.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "single non-inverting buffers (SN74LVC1G07), parts U15, U22, U35, U36"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "U15 | SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1 | ... MPN=U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "U15.1(/OE,input) ... U15.4(Y,output)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The sourced push-pull outputs can actively drive high where the specified open-drain outputs would release the line. That can change the e-stop sink behavior or cause contention in the shared e-stop wiring.",
      "confidence": 0.89
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The CAN transceiver ground and supply connections defeat the specified galvanic isolation. The e-stop buffer sourcing MPNs also identify a different output type from the specified open-drain parts, potentially changing the sink circuit’s behavior."
}

